Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:11:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Review round 4: the parallel test pins the fixes; a
 crossed fault is named

- The parallel test's distributed cases accept the split's own refusal of
  a chain running ALONG a seam (the ranks must still agree); they asserted
  "passed" and failed on every layout.
- The stray end is put on an edge the actual partition gives to two
  ranks (found from the point star-forest), so the case fails where the
  doubled edge hid the end; the kink case asserts, over the ranks, that
  the turn is a vertex of the chain.
- Whether a tip or turn label exists is reduced over the ranks before the
  gather: a rank without it hung the others.
- A chain cut beside both side labels of a fault the mesh does not record
  as split (a mesh read back from a file) is refused as a crossing of that
  fault, not with advice to resample.
- test_1174's junction pattern is the split's own message, so add_fault's
  handed-back refusal cannot satisfy it.

Suites: 435 passed, 1 skipped. The parallel test is for the reviewer.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
